# Juno Bank - Project Context

You are working on **Juno Bank**, a premium banking website for high net worth individuals (HNWI) and corporate clients.

## Tech Stack

| Technology      | Version | Purpose                        |
| --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------ |
| Next.js         | 16.x    | App Router framework           |
| React           | 19.x    | UI library                     |
| TypeScript      | 5.x     | Type safety (strict mode)      |
| Tailwind CSS    | 4.x     | Utility-first styling          |
| Radix UI        | latest  | Headless accessible components |
| Framer Motion   | 12.x    | Animations                     |
| React Hook Form | 7.x     | Form state management          |
| Zod             | 4.x     | Schema validation              |

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router
│   ├── api/          # API routes
│   ├── layout.tsx    # Root layout
│   └── page.tsx      # Homepage
├── components/
│   ├── ui/           # Reusable UI primitives
│   └── sections/     # Page sections
├── lib/
│   ├── utils.ts      # cn() helper
│   └── validations.ts # Zod schemas
└── types/            # TypeScript definitions
```

## Path Aliases

Use `@/*` for imports from `src/`:

```typescript
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
```

## Brand Guidelines

### Tone
- Sophisticated and professional
- Trustworthy and confident
- Exclusive but approachable

### Visual Style
- Minimalist and elegant
- Premium feel with generous whitespace
- Subtle animations for polish

### Design Principles
1. **Clarity** - Information hierarchy is immediately clear
2. **Elegance** - Every element serves a purpose
3. **Trust** - Visual cues that reinforce security
4. **Premium** - Details that signal quality and exclusivity
